.TH PATINA-SESSION 1 "2026-10-18" "patina-desktop 0.1.0" "Patina Desktop"
.SH NAME
patina-session \- start a Patina desktop session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patina-session
.RI [ COMMAND ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B patina-session
starts the Patina compositor with the top panel and the dock, inside a D-Bus session bus if
one is not already running, and starts the programs set to start with the session
(XDG autostart: \fI~/.config/autostart\fR and \fI/etc/xdg/autostart\fR).
It is what the "Patina" entry in a display manager's session list runs, and it can also be
run from a text console: switch to one with Ctrl+Alt+F3, log in, and run
.BR patina-session .
.PP
Each
.I COMMAND
is a shell command that the compositor starts after the panel, with
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
pointing at it.
.PP
The session runs the compositor on the display directly (DRM/KMS), so it must be started from
a login session on a seat, not from inside another graphical session.
Run inside one, the compositor opens in a window instead, which is useful for testing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WGPU_BACKEND
Graphics API used by the panel. Defaults to
.B gl
because it works on real GPUs and in virtual machines; software Vulkan cannot run the panel.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/patina/session.env
Optional shell fragment sourced before the session starts, for example
.RB \(lq WGPU_BACKEND=vulkan \(rq.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/patina/session.log
Output of the session. The previous log is kept as
.IR session.log.old .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR patina-compositor (1),
.BR patina-panel (1)
